From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:08:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Routing: plan around standing Sims, re-plan on object
 changes, unstick

Behind VMFeatures.DynamicObstacles (default on):
- Sims that are standing still (not walking a route, or waiting) are
  obstacles for the within-room planner, except near our start or goal.
  If that leaves no route, planning falls back to the old behaviour
  (walk up, wait or shoo).
- VMContext.RoomObjectVersion counts object placements/moves/removals
  per room (not carried objects). A walking Sim whose room changed plans
  the rest of its walk again at the next waypoint, keeping the old route
  if the new plan fails.
- A door whose portal function failed is tried once more after a 2 s
  wait when no other room route exists, instead of failing the goal.

Behind VMFeatures.Unstick (default on):
- A Sim standing inside the clearance of one or two objects (and nothing
  else) steps to the nearest free point within 1.5 tiles, preferring the
  goal direction, with a shimmy-style segment that may overlap those
  objects; the route continues from there. Previously every route
  failed with NoPath.

Behind VMFeatures.RoutingFixes:
- CanShooAvatar finds the top routing frame (the loop had no break).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
